      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. So it's more about the legal chain of responsibility. A lot of people I see online say those legal arguments are just excuses to avoid addressing historical harm, though. Do you think those specific legal/philosophical points are actually strong enough to stand up against the argument that the state's obligation is permanent, or are they mostly used as political tools to deflect?",
